    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, with the 3 new postcode acceptance tests plus the full suite green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional, region-validated `postcode` (4 digits) to the owner create/update flow.\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`), so it's carried on both request and response DTOs. Not in `required`, keeping the contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 new `postcode` field with getter/setter and `@Column(name = \"postcode\")`. MapStruct auto-maps it by name (DTO\u2194entity) in both directions, so no mapper changes were needed.\n- Added a nullable `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column to all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). For hsqldb (used by tests) the seed inserts are positional, so I placed the column at the end of the table and appended a `NULL` to each `INSERT INTO owners` in `db/hsqldb/data.sql`.\n\n**Validation (OfficeFloor pipeline)**\n- New step `RequirePostcode` \u2014 runs only when a postcode is present: rejects non-4-digit values, and for a known-region city (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099) rejects out-of-range values. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode. Absent postcode is skipped.\n- New checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + handler (400, `errors: [\"postcode\"]`) + escalation YAML, following the existing telephone/email pattern.\n- Wired the step into both `owners.POST.yml` (after field validation) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, and added `owner.setPostcode(...)` to `ApplyOwner` so updates persist the value.\n\nThe postcode is stored and returned verbatim (via GET `/api/owners/{id}`), and an owner created without one is still accepted.",
